# Build context for apps/api/Dockerfile (the context is the repository root).
#
# An ALLOW-list, not a deny-list: everything is excluded first and only what the image
# installs is let back in, so a new top-level directory (a dataset, an export, a graph,
# an agent worktree, a stray .env) can never reach the image or the Docker daemon by
# accident. In particular none of these can get in: .git, .venv, node_modules, .claude,
# graphify-out, logs/, projects/, exports/, tests and their data, *.sqlite3,
# config/config.yaml, and any .env* / *.pem / *.key file.
*

# Runtime dependency list + the two distributions the image installs (non-editable, into
# site-packages: the sandbox child runs `python -I`, which ignores PYTHONPATH).
!requirements.txt
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!uadas_core/
!apps/api/pyproject.toml
!apps/api/manage.py
!apps/api/uadas_api/

# Re-excluded inside the allowed directories.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-journal
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
